From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:02:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(selection): selectTeeth, getActiveTooth and
 onSelectionChange

A host could read the selection but not set it, and could only follow it
through onStateChange, which also fires on every chart edit.

- selectTeeth(teeth, { activeTooth }) selects from the host; unknown and
  duplicate numbers are ignored, [] clears; works in read-only mode
- getActiveTooth() returns the tooth the controls show
- onSelectionChange((teeth, activeTooth) => ...) fires only when either
  changes; a failing listener cannot break the others
- onStateChange keeps firing on selection changes

Tests: selection-api.test.ts; API surface golden re-captured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
